      "side": 1,
      "message": "Setting the socket options alone does not continuously activate AF_XDP busy polling: the kernel enters sk_busy_loop() through recvmsg(), while this datapath calls recvmsg() only during fill-ring replenishment. Once an idle fill ring is full, no syscall occurs, so the next burst remains interrupt-driven and SO_PREFER_BUSY_POLL can lapse. Could we issue a nonblocking recvmsg() when the RX ring is empty and busy polling is enabled, similar to DPDK\u0027s AF_XDP receive path?",
      "revId": "a4d1def8af97cd2e480b0764723dd9a9c9508b0e",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
